---
import { Heart } from "@lucide/astro"
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import sparkyImage from "../../assets/easter-eggs/sparky.webp";
---

<div class="flex flex-col gap-4" style="text-wrap: pretty;">
    <h2 class="font-sans text-3xl font-black">WHAT IS SPARKHACKS?</h2>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-8 h-[350px] overflow-y-scroll" style="scrollbar-color: gray #ffffff00;">
        <section class="flex flex-row justify-center align-center items-center gap-8">
            
            <p>
                <span class="font-bold">SparkHacks</span> is the University of Illinois Chicago's 24-hour hackathon where students create technology based projects. Starting in 2023, SparkHacks has become one of UIC's most active student-led tech experiences.
            </p>
            <Picture src={sparkyImage} alt="Sparky the Dragon." class="border-[4px] border-primary rounded-xl" />
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-row justify-center align-center items-center gap-8 pb-4">
            <Picture src={sparkyImage} alt="Sparky the Dragon." class="border-[4px] border-primary rounded-xl" />
            <p>
                SparkHacks was initially started by <span class="font-bold">Women in Computer Science (WiCS)</span> at UIC in 2022. 
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col justify-center align-center items-center gap-8 pb-4">
            <p class="mx-4">
                It was inspired by WiCS' annual tradition: <span class="font-bold">the Scavenger Hunt</span>. Students could compete against fellow students and professors for a chance to win prizes.
            </p>
            <p class="mx-4">
                People enjoyed the <span class="font-bold">community, competitiveness, and problem solving</span>. WiCS wanted to replicate that same energy but at a larger scale.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-row justify-center align-center items-center gap-8 pb-4">            
            <Picture src={sparkyImage} alt="Sparky the Dragon." class="border-[4px] border-primary rounded-xl" />
            <Picture src={sparkyImage} alt="Sparky the Dragon." class="border-[4px] border-primary rounded-xl" />
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col justify-center align-center items-center gap-8 pb-4">
            <p>
                Teamed with <span class="font-bold">ACM, SWE, LOGiCA, NSBE, and many more student organizations,</span> this event has been brought to life by the hard work and dedication of so many people. 
            </p>
            <p>
                Since then SparkHacks' purpose has been to <span class="font-bold">promote diversity, creativity, and innovation</span>.
            </p>
            
            <Picture src={sparkyImage} alt="Sparky the Dragon." class="border-[4px] border-primary rounded-xl" />
            
            <p>
                <span class="font-bold">Fun Facts!</span> SparkHacks was originally hosted in Student Center East (SCE) for the 2023-2024 iterations. It moved to the Academic & Residential Complex (ARC) in 2025, and finally in the Computer Design Research and Learning Center (CDRLC) in 2026! 
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
</div>